<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Consolidated Diamond year loss narrows.</title>
<headline>Consolidated Diamond year loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     9.23	  vs 12.00</p>
<p>    Loss for period	 6.92	  vs 9.00</p>
<p>    Loss at start of period 55.99     vs 46.99</p>
<p>    Loss at end of period 62.91	 vs 55.99</p>
<p>    Turnover		  nil	   vs nil</p>
<p>Full name: Consolidated Diamond Corp Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group, whose principal asset is the Samada diamond mine, said its operations there remained suspended.</p>
<p>It added that talks were continuing with the group's holding firm to increase its share capital by 15 million rand.</p>
<p>&quot;Should the outcome of these negotiations be successful, the recapitalisation will restore the group's solvency,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The firm could then go onto exercise various rights and options and acquire another diamond prospecting and exploration enterprise.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
